  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Food, Nutrition &amp; Livelihoods Security of women and men, including PLWHA in Maban County</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x201c;This is a CTP (CAFOD and Trocaire in Partnership) project&#x201d;.  The project will support IDPs and also host communities who are located near the IDP sites by distributing seeds and tools to enable them to meet their short term food requirements during the rainfall season. This is expected to ensure that the affected targeted group is able to improve their food security situation, by consuming the harvests and also sale if there are surplus. The short term project,4 month project will enable CDO Staff with support from CTP to procure, distribute, provide basic training and monitor the project outputs. CTP will provide PCM accompaniment support to CDO to ensure that the minimum project implementation standards are met. CTP will also the project inputs from Juba and also support in the delivery of the inputs to Maban.</narrative>
  </description>
